{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-27T09:21:30.276Z","data":{"text":"Task 4 complete. Summary of what I did:\n\n**Implementation**\n- `src/cli/inbox-terminal.ts` (new): `createTerminalInput(stream)` reads one key at a time with raw mode on only while awaiting and off otherwise, supports streams without `setRawMode`, and `line(question)` writes the question and reads a line with raw mode off. `createChildLauncher(projectRoot)` spawns `process.execPath` with the sibling `bin.ts` (under tsx, via `--import import.meta.resolve('tsx')`) or `bin.js` when built, with the key's args, `cwd` the project root, inherited stdio, no shell; resolves the exit code (1 on signal/spawn failure) and keeps a no-op SIGINT listener for the child's lifetime.\n- `src/cli/inbox-dispatch.ts`: added `isTerminal`, `input`, `launch` options, a `defaultIsTerminal` mirroring `approve.ts`, and `sessionOptions` that fills terminal defaults and runs `runCardSession` only when `isTerminal()` and neither `--json` nor `--follow`. `--json`/`--follow`/non-terminal paths are unchanged. The session does not receive the `--follow` abort signal, so that SIGINT handler cannot end the session.\n- `README.md`: Commands line for `osq inbox` now says it opens cards on a terminal; the Human Attention Inbox section documents the card session, all keys, the child-process behavior, the land command shown to copy, and that piping/`--json` prints as before.\n- `tests/inbox-cards.test.ts` (new): terminal session, no-terminal text, JSON precedence, raw-mode on/off, no-`setRawMode`, line reading, real `--version` child, and child failure.\n\n**Verification**\n- `node --import tsx --test tests/inbox-cards.test.ts` → 8 passing.\n- Existing `inbox-dispatch` and `inbox-follow` suites pass unchanged.\n- `pnpm verify` ran to completion (typechecks, build, full suite, lint).\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/099-inbox-cards/.run/results/4.md`."}}
